{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "lockout-lock-removal",
  "title": "Removing someone else's lock",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "f0723fa2-bc69-4a56-bc9f-702bcfbb2cea",
      "question": "Under the lockout/tagout procedure, who may remove a lock applied by an authorized employee who is not on site, and what must happen before they do?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-04T05:33:19.426384Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-04T05:33:23.869772Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Who may remove the lock**\nOnly the **Plant EHS Manager** (or a **deputy named in writing**) may remove a lock applied by an authorized employee who is not on site. This is an exceptional case allowed only when the machine must be returned to service [1].\n\n**What must happen before removal**\nAll of the following steps must be completed:\n\n1. The **Maintenance Supervisor** has verified the employee is not on site and has made **at least two documented attempts to reach them by phone**.\n2. The **Plant EHS Manager** has confirmed the machine is **safe to re-energize** and that **no one is working on it**.\n3. The absent employee **is informed that the lock was removed** before they return to work on that machine.\n4. The removal is **recorded in the lockout log** with the names of everyone involved and the reason [1].\n\n*Note: This is a synthetic demonstration document (SAF-SOP-007, Rev C) — not for operational use.*\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — lockout_tagout_sop.pdf — evidence `hermes-receipt:2f136520ff1a6e61ba6bbb498a50946b1ece47bd4216b9cce7813a3f0feb19c0`",
        "citations": [
