            "collection": "knowledge",
            "collectionVersion": "knowledge__v1",
            "hits": [
              {
                "rank": 1,
                "score": 3.80859375,
                "vectorScore": 0.5370785593986511,
                "sourceId": "manufacturing.procedures",
                "documentId": "manufacturing.procedures:f-67a5daa3d77e97fb",
                "chunkId": "manufacturing.procedures:f-67a5daa3d77e97fb:0009",
                "title": "lockout_tagout_sop.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Lockout/Tagout of Machinery Energy Sources\nStandard operating procedure for servicing and maintenance\n7. Removal of a lock by someone else\nOnly the person who applied a lock may remove it. Supervisors, co-workers and contractors may not cut or remove another person’s lock.\nIn the exceptional case that the authorized employee is not on site and the machine must be returned to service, only the Plant EHS Manager (or a deputy named in writing) may remove the lock, and only after all of these steps:\n- The Maintenance Supervisor has verified that the employee is not on site and has made at least two documented attempts to reach them by phone.\n- The Plant EHS Manager has confirmed that the machine is safe to re-energize and that no one is working on it.\n- The employee is told that the lock was removed before they return to work on that machine.\n- The removal is entered in the lockout log, with the names of the people involved and the reason.\nCNC Mill, Energy sources = Electrical main supply; pneumatic air; coolant and lubrication pumps; stored energy in servo drives. CNC Mill, Isolating devices and checks = Main disconnect; air supply valve with dump; pump breakers; wait 5 minutes for drive discharge. CNC Lathe, Energy sources = Electrical main supply; hydraulic chuck and turret power pack; pneumatic air; coolant pump. CNC Lathe, Isolating devices and checks = Main disconnect; hydraulic power pack breaker and bleed; air supply valve with dump. Hydraulic Press, Energy sources = Elec",
