                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Lockout/Tagout of Machinery Energy Sources\nStandard operating procedure for servicing and maintenance\n9. Training, audits and records\n- (\\bullet) Authorized employees are trained and certified before their first lockout, and are retrained every 12 months and whenever the procedure or the machine changes.\n- (\\bullet) Affected employees are trained to recognize a lock and tag and never to start or operate a locked-out machine.\n- (\\bullet) The Plant EHS Manager audits this procedure for each machine type once a year. The audit is carried out by an authorized employee who is not using the procedure in the audit, and findings are closed within 30 days.\n- (\\bullet) The lockout log is kept for three years. Personal locks are red and identify their owner; no lock may be used for any other purpose.\nRev A, Date = 3 March 2021. Rev A, Change = First release.. Rev B, Date = 20 September 2023. Rev B, Change = Added group lockbox and shift change rules.. Rev C, Date = 15 January 2026. Rev C, Change = Added robot cells; clarified lock removal by the Plant EHS Manager (section 7); added annual audit independence.",
